{
  "requirement": "Every source text the harness supplies to a model, including mandatory inputs,\n`habeas` reads, and `ripgrep` results, and every source text Habeas displays in\nthe book or `habeas info`, MUST be redacted:\n\n1. In a workspace `habeas.toml` or user configuration file, the value of every\n   explicit credential field defined by {cite}`requirements.authoring.credentials`\n   MUST be replaced. Such a file that is not valid TOML MUST be replaced whole,\n   with `configuration` as the kind, because its fields cannot be located.\n2. In every source, each match of a built-in rule of the `secretshape` crate MUST\n   be replaced. The replaced region MUST be extended through each adjacent region\n   that the crate's entropy heuristic flags and that only whitespace separates\n   from the region, repeating until no flagged region is adjacent. The heuristic\n   MUST NOT cause redaction on its own.\n\nA replacement MUST read `[REDACTED:<kind>]`, where `<kind>` is the credential\nfield or the rule's name, and MUST keep every line break within the replaced\ntext, so line numbers are unchanged. Outlines MUST be built from the original\nsource, and the structural hash MUST hash each text piece that overlaps a\nredacted region in its redacted form, so evidence never depends on a credential's\nvalue and redaction never changes or breaks a file's outline. The `secretshape` version MUST be pinned exactly; upgrading\nit MAY change redaction and hashes and MUST be treated as a deliberate change.",
  "determination": false,
  "rationale": "## Verdict\n\nMost of the redaction obligations are implemented and tested. Three gaps remain, and none carries a {fixme}, so the determination is false.\n\n## Obligations mapped to code and tests\n\n- **Credential fields replaced by name (obligation 1).**\n  - Code: `src/redaction.rs` `of_file`, `is_configuration_file(_for)`, `configuration_regions`, `credential_fields`, `item_fields` and `value_fields`.\n  - Tests: `configuration_credential_fields_are_redacted_by_name_whatever_their_values`, `the_user_configuration_file_and_its_aliases_are_configuration_files`, and the `habeas.toml` read in `model_inputs_reads_searches_and_citation_prompts_are_redacted`.\n- **Invalid TOML replaced whole as `configuration`.**\n  - Code: `configuration_regions`.\n  - Test: `invalid_configuration_files_are_redacted_whole_keeping_lines`.\n- **Every `secretshape` rule match replaced (obligation 2).**\n  - Code: `secret_regions`, `scanners`, `merge`.\n  - Tests: `tokens_in_code_are_redacted_without_adjacent_code`, `private_keys_are_redacted_from_header_through_body_keeping_lines`.\n- **Extension through whitespace-adjacent heuristic-flagged regions.**\n  - Code: the forward and backward loops in `secret_regions`.\n  - Tests: the private-key tests and `regions_extend_backward_keep_crlf_and_scan_past_a_mebibyte`.\n- **The heuristic alone never redacts.**\n  - Code: `secret_regions` returns early when the rule-only scan finds nothing.\n  - Test: `heuristic_findings_alone_are_not_redacted`.\n- **`[REDACTED:<kind>]` replacements that keep every line break.**\n  - Code: `Redaction::slice` and `push_line_breaks`.\n  - Tests: the redaction tests cover line counts, CRLF and multi-line values.\n- **Outlines built from the original source, with redacted hash pieces.**\n  - Code: `parse_redacted`, `Builder::piece`, `Builder::encode` and `plain_text` in `src/outline/mod.rs`.\n  - Tests: `redaction_never_changes_an_outline`, `hashes_do_not_depend_on_credential_values`, `slices_concatenate_to_the_redacted_whole`.\n- **Delivery of redacted text to the model.**\n  - Code: `OutlineCache::parse`, `node_range`, `InputSelector::resolve`, `model_citations_value`, `initial_prompt`.\n  - Test: `model_inputs_reads_searches_and_citation_prompts_are_redacted` covers mandatory inputs, `habeas` reads, `ripgrep` and citation commentary; `ast_grep_returns_innermost_nodes_...` covers `ast_grep`.\n- **Display in the book and `habeas info`.**\n  - Code: `render_detail_sections` and `render_input` in `src/index.rs`.\n  - Test: `detail_pages_and_info_display_redacted_source` covers the definition text, an outline node, the recorded requirements text and `habeas.toml`.\n- **`secretshape` pinned exactly.** `Cargo.toml` pins `secretshape = \"=0.1.0\"`. This is declarative, so it needs no test.\n\n## Gaps\n\n1. **Site prompt redaction is untested.**\n   - Code: `SiteItem::matches_value` in `src/sites.rs` (lines 86–109) has an {impl} for the requirement. It redacts the text of a violation match with `redact_text`, and that conditional is its own transformation.\n   - Tests: no test gives it a credential-shaped violation text. The only test that touches it, `sites_are_the_innermost_nodes_of_site_matches_and_violations_within_them`, uses `panic!(\"z\")`, and it has no {test} reference to this requirement.\n   - Result: the site-prompt path to the model, which the requirement's \"every source text the harness supplies to a model\" covers, is unverified.\n\n2. **A test of GitHub redaction is not marked.**\n   - Code: `src/github.rs` `fetch` carries an {impl} for this requirement and redacts the issue title and body.\n   - Test: `the_tool_reads_issues_with_the_token_and_redacts_bodies` (lines 741–797) asserts the token is redacted in the tool result and in the cache. It carries only a {test} for `requirements.authoring.github_reads`, with none for `requirements.authoring.redaction`.\n   - Result: a test that verifies this requirement lacks its {test} marking.\n\n3. **Redaction on two displayed paths is untested.**\n   - Code: `render_detail_sections` redacts validation findings (`redact_text` over `detail_evidence.errors`) and the \"Unreadable evidence record\" JSON. `render_input` redacts its fallback text for unresolved inputs.\n   - Tests: `detail_pages_and_info_display_redacted_source` passes `errors: &[]`, a readable record and resolvable inputs, so none of these branches runs with a credential.\n   - Result: output the requirement governs along separate code paths has no test on those paths.\n\nNo {fixme} references to this requirement were found among the inputs, so none of these gaps is acknowledged.",
